{
  "note": "Phase 1128 — the platform-baseline capability wave (Media text tracks #1110, Embed #1111, the tooltip trait #1112, Combobox #1113, Tree #1120), driven through the C-ABI on BOTH targets. The native leg is tests/platform_baseline_abi.rs; the wasm32 leg is js/platform-baseline.mjs. This matters beyond this repo: fuaran-swift and fuaran-kt are decode-only render projections over this core, so whatever the ABI does not expose, they cannot reach — and 'the server path does the right thing' is therefore not the claim that needs making.",
  "oracle": "Every `tree` is the SHARED CORPUS fixture verbatim, and `expectTree` is the same bytes — so the round-trip leg is certified against wire-format-fixtures, not against this file. The render expectations are drawn from the NORMATIVE obligations in WIRE_FORMAT.md (3.6.6 / 3.6.8 / 3.6.9 / 3.6.12 and the tooltip trait in 3.6), and whether this host MEETS them is settled by tests/render_obligations.rs against render-fidelity.json. This file records envelopes, not truth: its job is to hold the two TARGETS to identical bytes for identical inputs.",
  "egressNote": "The C-ABI session opens under deny_non_local_egress and exposes no policy knob, so a remote Embed source is REFUSED on this path. That is not an artefact of the fixture — it is what a Swift or Kotlin surface over this core actually gets, and the embed case pins it deliberately: title and sandbox survive, the source is omitted, and the refusal is recorded under the embed's own class.",
